bed by its inhabitants as a prison rather than a shelter.</p><p>Through interviews with current residents, Polsterâ€™s film weaves a sobering tapestry of experiences â€“ in spite of the centreâ€™s resistance to the documentary project. Many asylum seekers speak of poor living conditions, lack of access to legal support, and the impossibility of social integration due to the campâ€™s remote location. Their legal limbo, caused by excessive delays in application processing, leads to further psychological distress. In one heartbreaking scene, a detainee looks wistfully at the cattle herds that graze nearby, envious of their freedom of movement. With strict curfew hours and few recreational activities on offer, time at the BÃ¼rglkopf camp stretches on seemingly infinitely.</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/jul/20/out-of-sight-review-asylum-seekers-alps">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;TVmnNFQzXp8KqTzmAPTJ2gx9bwhbENcP1cjkVEQusuEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;TTxOLMhbswtfEjEPzyJysGUJRFOFmEop3Q5zKmkg4eoƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;xe5Xd8eblTBm7-x6aFM4AaSvb2q8hOeKrLohPcsHQJoƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;KgiU-7sV9r-qMq90jO0guRogrPXxvDhXcNbcXXRgPr4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;G8XTxbAS6fjYI5dBZdFQbefn99DFZ0VgG4W8ykj1YLIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;lu6pIvjD27ctiZFTjNuzwvFcVhLeY9e7tc_WxSCnk9cƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ux1tpJX4_moYiFmVI71dqI2b4JCHCZ4aJ6qeCs